description:
## Problem

`app.clipboard.pasteImage` (`ctrl+v`) is dispatched but octo_pi has no clipboard read. Upstream behavior: read OS clipboard for image data, write to a temp PNG, **insert the path string at cursor** (does not embed bytes).

## Upstream behavior (`interactive-mode.ts:2374-2399`)

```ts
this.defaultEditor.onPasteImage = () => {
  this.handleClipboardImagePaste();
};

private async handleClipboardImagePaste(): Promise<void> {
  try {
    const image = await readClipboardImage();
    if (!image) return;
    const ext = extensionForImageMimeType(image.mimeType) ?? "png";
    const fileName = `pi-clipboard-${crypto.randomUUID()}.${ext}`;
    const filePath = path.join(os.tmpdir(), fileName);
    fs.writeFileSync(filePath, Buffer.from(image.bytes));
    this.editor.insertTextAtCursor?.(filePath);
    this.ui.requestRender();
  } catch {
    // Silently ignore clipboard errors
  }
}
```

`readClipboardImage()` is OS-specific:
- **macOS**: `pbpaste` with `-Prefer png` flag, or AppleScript `osascript -e 'the clipboard as «class PNGf»'`.
- **Linux**: `xclip -selection clipboard -t image/png -o` (X11) or `wl-paste --type image/png` (Wayland).
- **Windows**: native API.

## Files likely created/modified

- New: `OctoPi.TUI.Clipboard` module — likely a port to a CLI tool (`pbpaste` etc.) initially; NIF later if needed.
- Update: `apps/octo_pi_tui/lib/octo_pi/tui/interactive.ex` `app.clipboard.pasteImage` handler.

## Acceptance

- With an image on clipboard, `ctrl+v` writes a temp PNG to `System.tmp_dir!()` and inserts its absolute path into the editor at cursor.
- With no image (clipboard has text or is empty), `ctrl+v` is a **silent no-op** (no warning per upstream — matches `try/catch{}` swallowing).
- macOS path verified.

## Default key on Windows

Upstream uses `alt+v` on Windows (`coding-agent/src/core/keybindings.ts:107`):
```ts
"app.clipboard.pasteImage": {
  defaultKeys: process.platform === "win32" ? "alt+v" : "ctrl+v",
  ...
}
```
Mirror this in our defaults if octo_pi ever supports Windows. For now `ctrl+v` is fine.

## Notes

Larger surface than it looks because of platform shims. Suggest macOS-only first iteration; document as platform-gated. The path-as-text insertion (rather than image embedding) is intentional — the agent reads the file when it sees the path in the prompt.
